Title: Implementation of a Zero-Dependency Audio Codec using Templated Inlining

Contribution:

I have successfully implemented a zero-dependency audio codec (AudioCodec.cpp) using the C++17 standard's template and inlining features. The codec encodes audio input into a lossless, 16-bit PCM format without any external library dependencies.

The benchmark metric for this contribution is the encoding and decoding time measured in milliseconds (ms) on a standard PC, using the `chrono` library. The target audio input has a sample rate of 48kHz, a bit depth of 16-bit, and a duration of 10 seconds.

Audio/Visual Parameters:

- Bit rate: 1,474,560 bits per second (16-bit PCM)
- Sample rate: 48,000 samples per second
- Duration: 10 seconds
- Channels: Mono
- BPM: Not applicable (as this is a pure audio application)

Code Snippet (AudioCodec.cpp):

```cpp
